<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mopsus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mopsus is a legendary seer of Greek tradition, said to be a son of Manto and grandson of Tiresias, who defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calchas">Calchas</a> in a contest of prophecy and led migrants into southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a>. Cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamphylia">Pamphylia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, such as Perge and Mopsuestia, honoured him as founder. A Luwian–Phoenician inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karatepe">Karatepe</a> names a dynasty of the 'house of Mopsus'.</p></div>
